      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "aside_text",
          "bbox": [
            0.055,
            0.584,
            0.078,
            0.848
          ],
          "content": "Curiosity | Textbook of Science | Grade 7"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.271,
            0.081,
            0.857,
            0.154
          ],
          "content": "We have noticed shadows of ourselves and other objects around us when we are in the Sun or under a light (Fig. 11.7). Also, you might have had fun making different shapes with shadows sometime."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.272,
            0.155,
            0.857,
            0.229
          ],
          "content": "Do translucent and transparent objects create shadows or not? Did you **notice** that in Activity 11.3? Opaque objects form darker shadows. Translucent objects make lighter shadows. Even some transparent objects can create faint shadows!"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.272,
            0.229,
            0.582,
            0.248
          ],
          "content": "Let us learn more about shadows."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.287,
            0.262,
            0.55,
            0.283
          ],
          "content": "**Activity 11.4: Let us explore**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.282,
            0.294,
            0.832,
            0.314
          ],
          "content": "Collect some opaque objects of different shapes and sizes."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.283,
            0.316,
            0.856,
            0.351
          ],
          "content": "Repeat Activity 11.3, but this time, carry out the actions mentioned in the first column of Table 11.2."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.282,
            0.353,
            0.856,
            0.39
          ],
          "content": "**Observe** the shape and size of the shadow on the screen for each of the actions."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.272,
            0.392,
            0.856,
            0.428
          ],
          "content": "Did the shadow form in all cases? Was the shape and size of the shadow the same as the object?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.282,
            0.43,
            0.855,
            0.449
          ],
          "content": "**Record** your observations in the second column of Table 11.2."
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.275,
            0.48,
            0.865,
            0.786
          ],
          "content": "<table><tr><td>Action</td><td>Observations regardingshadow</td></tr><tr><td>The screen is removed.</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>The object is removed.</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>The torch is switched off.</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>The object is moved closer to the screen,keeping the torch and the screen fixed.</td><td></td></tr><tr><td rowspan=3>The object is moved closer to the torchkeeping the torch and the screen fixed.The object is tilted, keeping the torch andthe screen fixed.The colour of the object is changed.</td><td></td></tr><tr><td></td></tr><tr><td></td></tr></table>",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.282,
                0.457,
                0.613,
                0.478
              ],
              "content": "Table 11.2: Observation of shadows"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_5_table_11.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.271,
            0.793,
            0.857,
            0.849
          ],
          "content": "What **conclusions** do you draw from this activity? What do we need to observe a shadow? Does the colour of the shadow change when the colour of the object is changed?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.272,
            0.849,
            0.857,
            0.888
          ],
          "content": "Shadows are formed when an object blocks light from falling on a screen. We need a source of light, an opaque object, and a screen"
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.002,
